      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0361",
      "sequence": 373,
      "meaning": "The wise Vāmadeva, guru of Raghu’s line, again recounts the story of Viśvāmitra. Hearing the sage’s noble fame, Daśaratha inwardly describes the power of his own merit. With permission the people return and the king goes home with his sons, while Rāma’s wedding is sung everywhere and its pure renown fills the three worlds. From the day Rāma returned home married, joy has dwelt in Ayodhyā. Neither Sarasvatī nor Śeṣa can describe the celebration; knowing the glory of Rāma and Sītā to be a purifying treasury of auspiciousness and the very life of poets, Tulsīdāsa says he has told a little of it to sanctify his own speech.",
